<!--ID=B7267351-473F-409D-9765-754A8EBCDE05;Version=1|{"VoiceNameToIdMapItems":[{"Id":"f1b99834-fbfc-4d32-846d-c4dbd3050c19","Name":"Microsoft Server Speech Text to Speech Voice (en-GB, OllieMultilingualNeural)","ShortName":"en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural","Locale":"en-GB","VoiceType":"StandardVoice"}]}-->
<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.75%" pitch="-2.60%">
      A priest was going down that road.<break time="1000ms"/>
      A priest: a man set apart for sacred service, for the care of holy things.<break time="500ms"/>
      A man whose life was organized around God's purposes.<break time="1800ms"/>

      He saw the man lying in the road.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The text does not say he failed to notice.<break time="500ms"/>
      He saw.<break time="500ms"/>
      And he passed by on the other side.<break time="1800ms"/>

      The story does not tell us what he thought in that moment.<break time="500ms"/>
      It does not explain or excuse.<break time="500ms"/>
      It only says: he saw, and he passed by on the other side.<break time="1000ms"/>
      He put distance between himself and what he had seen.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Then a Levite came to the place.<break time="500ms"/>
      A Levite: another man of religious life, a servant of the temple, one who knew the law.<break time="500ms"/>
      He came and looked at the man.<break time="1000ms"/>
      And he too passed by on the other side.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Two men.<break time="500ms"/>
      Both from the world of religious knowledge and holy service.<break time="500ms"/>
      Both traveling the same road.<break time="500ms"/>
      Both seeing the same man.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Both choosing the other side.<break time="1800ms"/>

      There is no accusation in the story's tone.<break time="500ms"/>
      No editorial judgment is spoken aloud.<break time="500ms"/>
      The story simply shows what happened.<break time="1000ms"/>
      They saw. They chose not to stop.<break time="1800ms"/>

      The man lay in the road still.<break time="500ms"/>
      The dust settled back into stillness.<break time="500ms"/>
      The road was quiet again.<break time="1000ms"/>
      And then another figure came around the bend.<break time="1800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
